# Optional WSL WebUI operations layer

This rendered directory is an optional Phase 2b extension. It does not own the
application service, SSH, credentials, certificates, or Windows LAN rules.

- Application: `__APP_NAME_TEXT__` (`__APP_ID__`)
- User service observed by health checks: `__SERVICE_UNIT__`
- Application origin: `http://127.0.0.1:__APP_PORT__`
- Health path: `__HEALTH_PATH_TEXT__`
- Gateway: `https://__GATEWAY_HOSTNAME__:__GATEWAY_PORT__`, bound to `127.0.0.1`

The rendered gateway hostname is an internal server value. The client-facing
URL should use the canonical `https://APP_ID.SERVER_NAME.local/` form through
the Windows HTTPS relay; do not distribute the loopback gateway port.

The installer creates private gateway configuration, Caddy data, and Caddy
state directories with mode `700`. Create
`%h/.config/webui-gateway/gateway.env` with mode `600`. It must define
`GATEWAY_USERNAME` and `GATEWAY_PASSWORD_HASH`. Do not put
the password, password hash, certificates, private keys, or application secrets
in this directory or in `registry.json`.

The installer does not enable or start units. After independently verifying the
application loopback endpoint and creating the private environment file, an
operator may explicitly enable `webui-gateway.service` and
`wsl-app-health@__APP_ID__.timer`. LAN exposure requires a separate reviewed
Windows gateway step. Never register or forward the unauthenticated workbench on
port 4173.
